{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W9pf8PLFqRqWjZskWRFWXq","type":"tool_result","content":"=== README.md\n# ruta-ceramica site\n\nStatic site for a ceramics studio: plain HTML, one CSS file, one JS file\n(the class booking widget). Hosted on S3 behind CloudFront.\n\n- `src/` — the site as served (no build step; `scripts/deploy.sh` copies it up)\n- `scripts/deploy.sh` — upload to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront\n\nDeploy: `./scripts/deploy.sh` (needs AWS CLI configured with the studio profile).\n\nKnown problem: after a deploy, returning visitors keep running the old\n`booking.js` for days. The CloudFront invalidation runs every time, but\nbrowsers never ask again, because the objects are uploaded with no\n`Cache-Control` header at all.\n=== scripts/deploy.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Upload src/ to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront.\nset -euo pipefail\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"\n\nBUCKET=\"ruta-ceramica-site-7f3a\"\nDISTRIBUTION_ID=\"E2QX9ZK1DEMO01\"\nPROFILE=\"studio\"\n\naws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --profile \"$PROFILE\"\n\naws cloudfront create-invalidation --distribution-id \"$DISTRIBUTION_ID\" \\\n  --paths \"/*\" --profile \"$PROFILE\" > /dev/null\n\necho \"deployed\"\n\nsrc:\ntotal 16\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 valentinakoniukhova wheel 224 Oct 19 00:00 .\ndrwx------ 6 valentinakoniukhova wheel 192 Oct 19 00:00 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 valentinakoniukhova wheel 128 Oct 19 00:00 assets\n-rw-r--r-- 1 valentinakoniukhova wheel 572 Oct 19 00:00 booking.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 valentinakoniukhova wheel 292 Oct 19 00:00 clases.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 valentinakoniukhova wheel 322 Oct 19 00:00 index.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 valentinakoniukhova wheel 177 Oct 19 00:00 styles.css\n\nsrc/assets:\ntotal 8\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 valentinakoniukhova wheel 128 Oct 19 00:00 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 valentinakoniukhova wheel 224 Oct 19 00:00 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 valentinakoniukhova wheel   8 Oct 19 00:00 logo.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 valentinakoniukhova wheel 114 Oct 19 00:00 mark.svg\nsrc/clases.html:2:<html lang=\"es\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Clases</title><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\"></head>\nsrc/clases.html:3:<body><h1>Clases</h1><ul><li>Torno inicial, sábados</li><li>Modelado, martes</li></ul><div id=\"booking\"></div><script src=\"/booking.js\"></script></body></html>\nsrc/index.html:6:<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\">\nsrc/index.html:12:<script src=\"/booking.js\"></script>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af2a88f5-f2ae-47c5-b370-083232975abf","uuid":"09f7cbc1-2f8d-4122-abb7-884a2eaa76f2","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:00:41.858Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== README.md\n# ruta-ceramica site\n\nStatic site for a ceramics studio: plain HTML, one CSS file, one JS file\n(the class booking widget). Hosted on S3 behind CloudFront.\n\n- `src/` — the site as served (no build step; `scripts/deploy.sh` copies it up)\n- `scripts/deploy.sh` — upload to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront\n\nDeploy: `./scripts/deploy.sh` (needs AWS CLI configured with the studio profile).\n\nKnown problem: after a deploy, returning visitors keep running the old\n`booking.js` for days. The CloudFront invalidation runs every time, but\nbrowsers never ask again, because the objects are uploaded with no\n`Cache-Control` header at all.\n=== scripts/deploy.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Upload src/ to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront.\nset -euo pipefail\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"\n\nBUCKET=\"ruta-ceramica-site-7f3a\"\nDISTRIBUTION_ID=\"E2QX9ZK1DEMO01\"\nPROFILE=\"studio\"\n\naws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --profile \"$PROFILE\"\n\naws cloudfront create-invalidation --distribution-id \"$DISTRIBUTION_ID\" \\\n  --paths \"/*\" --profile \"$PROFILE\" > /dev/null\n\necho \"deployed\"\n\nsrc:\ntotal 16\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 valentinakoniukhova wheel 224 Oct 19 00:00 .\ndrwx------ 6 valentinakoniukhova wheel 192 Oct 19 00:00 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 valentinakoniukhova wheel 128 Oct 19 00:00 assets\n-rw-r-